      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Natural Resources"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Fossil fuels like coal, petroleum, and natural gas are exhaustible natural resources formed from dead organisms under high pressure and temperature over millions of years.",
        "Coke is a tough, porous, black substance and is an almost pure form of carbon used in steel manufacturing.",
        "Petroleum refining separates crude oil into fractions like LPG, petrol, kerosene, diesel, lubricating oil, and paraffin wax based on boiling points.",
        "Compressed Natural Gas (CNG) is a clean fuel stored under high pressure and causes significantly less air pollution than liquid fossil fuels.",
        "Combustion requires three necessary conditions: a combustible substance, air/oxygen, and attainment of the ignition temperature."
      ],
      "id": "t22ommy"
    },
